`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Measure: loss is not a score"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"A score is a protocol"}),`
`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Every way to choose N and D fits one playbook",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"From here on, N counts a model's parameters, D its training tokens and C its training compute in FLOPs. Week 2 wrote the tokens as T, and Week 6 used N for the number of GPUs, so in this lecture N always means parameters."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Choosing N and D for a run you can afford only once depends on a chain of three links. The compute budget constrains N and D, because every token costs compute and a larger model costs more per token. Under a training recipe kept comparable across runs, N and D predict the final loss. A benchmark protocol then maps the model's behavior on a task to a score."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The last link is the fragile one. Compute maps to loss through a smooth regularity that a fit can follow. The map from the loss on a task to the accuracy reported on it is loose, and it depends on how the score is computed."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The sweep trains small models under one comparable recipe. Week 5's warmup-stable-decay (WSD) schedule lets the runs of one model size share most of their compute. The fit finds the best model size at each budget and extrapolates it to a larger budget, and a held-out run checks that forecast. At the measurement step, a low loss can still fail to become a good benchmark score, and a score means something only together with the protocol that produced it."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Each approach you might try belongs to one step of this playbook. Extending the trend of small models to the target budget is the fit and the extrapolation. Training several sizes at one budget and keeping the best is a sweep, and a fit at each budget reads off the best size. A rule of thumb for tokens per parameter summarizes such fits, and data can test it. Keeping the small runs comparable is a condition on the sweep. Trying the forecast on a medium-sized run first is the held-out check. Asking whether a low loss means a good model is the measurement step."})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"Two new modules: fit and measure",accent:5,number:"5",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
