`]}),e.jsx(j,{week:7,density:"compact"}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"The exercise fits a sweep and measures under two protocols",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["This week the evaluation package of your codebase gains two modules. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"evaluation/scaling.py"})," takes the final losses of a sweep and fits loss against model size at each fixed compute budget. It then fits a power law to the best sizes and extrapolates it. ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"evaluation/benchmarks.py"})," stores the setup of each evaluation next to its score, so that anyone can repeat the measurement."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"With the two modules you run the Llama 3 playbook in miniature. The exercise produces four observable outputs: a sweep ledger, a fit of the best model size per budget, the error of the prediction for a held-out run, and a benchmark comparison under two documented protocols."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"In the pipeline map, this week's stage, Evaluation, links back to Pretraining, because scaling laws decide how compute is allocated before a run starts. The map carries no measurements."})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{reading:!0,title:"Sweep points run as independent jobs",accent:6,number:"6",items:"3",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Most sweep points: small, independent jobs"}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Run them in parallel on the scheduler"}),`
