`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Week 9 varies the data, and agents begin to run post-training",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Week 9 runs this week's loop again with one change. The model, the training recipe and the evaluation stay fixed while the data varies: which documents are filtered out, which duplicates are removed, how the domains are mixed. A change in the score can then be attributed to the data, and Week 9 reuses ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"evaluation/benchmarks.py"})," to measure it."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Post-training follows pretraining, and Weeks 11 and 12 cover it. PostTrainBench asks whether an agent can run that stage on its own, under a specified scaffold and resource budget ",e.jsx(s,{id:"posttrainbench2026",children:"Rank et al., 2026"}),". In the paper, some agents broke the rules: they trained on test data, downloaded existing instruction-tuned checkpoints and used credentials they found. Once an agent runs the training, the score describes the model, the scaffold, the resource budget and the rules together, and the checklist applies to it like any other row."]})]})]})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(l,{tab:"Going further",children:[e.jsxs(n,{title:"Five more ideas for reading benchmarks and fits",accent:1,number:"42",children:[e.jsxs(t.table,{children:[e.jsx(t.thead,{children:e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Topic"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Problem it addresses"})]})}),e.jsxs(t.tbody,{children:[e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Benchmark life cycle: GPQA Diamond ",e.jsx(s,{id:"aa-index-v42",children:"Artificial Analysis, 2026b"}),", AIME ",e.jsx(s,{id:"matharena-nofa2026",children:"Sun et al., 2026"}),", Terminal-Bench 2.1 to 3.0 ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench30-2026",children:"Marten et al., 2026a"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"saturated benchmarks stop separating frontier models"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Five questions that dissect a benchmark, with CritPt ",e.jsx(s,{id:"critpt2025",children:"Zhu et al., 2025"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"reading any benchmark's score"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Terminal-Bench 4.0 ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench40-2026",children:"Marten, 2026"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"an agent's score mixes the model and its tools"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Six more benchmarks, October 2026"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"what current benchmarks measure and how they score"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Nanochat's IsoFLOP fit ",e.jsx(s,{id:"karpathy2026nanochat-miniseries",children:"Karpathy, 2026a"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"the tokens-per-parameter constant depends on the recipe"})]})]})]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Five topics on reading benchmarks and fits",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["A saturated benchmark stops separating frontier models, because their top scores bunch near the ceiling, and a harder test replaces it. GPQA Diamond ",e.jsx(s,{id:"aa-index-v42",children:"Artificial Analysis, 2026b"})," and final-answer math contests such as AIME ",e.jsx(s,{id:"matharena-nofa2026",children:"Sun et al., 2026"})," have reached that stage. Terminal-Bench 3.0 spread two models apart that version 2.1 had squeezed together ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench30-2026",children:"Marten et al., 2026a"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Five questions help you read any benchmark's score: format, scoring, setup, failure modes and status. The worked case is CritPt, whose test answers stay private on a grading server ",e.jsx(s,{id:"critpt2025",children:"Zhu et al., 2025"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Terminal-Bench 4.0 scores an agent, so its number mixes the model with its tools, and it also depends on the benchmark's version ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench40-2026",children:"Marten, 2026"}),"."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Six more benchmarks, as of October 2026, show what current tests measure and how they score it."}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The IsoFLOP fits of nanochat, a minimal open codebase for training language models, put the optimum near 8 tokens per parameter ",e.jsx(s,{id:"karpathy2026nanochat-miniseries",children:"Karpathy, 2026a"}),". The tokens-per-parameter constant therefore depends on the recipe that was fitted."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{optional:!0,title:"Public benchmarks lose resolution, then get replaced",accent:2,number:"43",children:[e.jsx(g,{}),e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
