`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["Version 4.0: 66 tasks, 8 removed, 19 fixed ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench40-2026",children:"Marten, 2026"})]}),`
`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"A Terminal-Bench score belongs to a model, an agent and a version",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Terminal-Bench gives an agent a multi-step task in a sandboxed terminal. The agent works in its own container until it finishes or times out. The task's tests then run in a separate verifier container, which checks the end state the agent left behind. No judge model is involved. Keeping the two containers apart blocks many ways of hacking the reward ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench30-2026",children:"Marten et al., 2026a"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The benchmark measures an agent, and an ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"agent = model + scaffold"}),". The scaffold is the program around the model, such as Claude Code or Codex. It decides what the model sees, which tools it may call and when it stops. A score therefore mixes the model's capability with the scaffold's, unless the scaffold is held fixed and reported. Leaderboard submissions must use the default resources, run at least five trials per task, and score an errored trial as 0 ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench-leaderboard",children:"Terminal-Bench Team, n.d."}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Version 4.0, released on 2026-08-28, removed 8 tasks, among them saturated ones, ones models refused and ones with public solutions ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench40-2026",children:"Marten, 2026"}),". It fixed 19 tasks and gave every task a flat agent timeout of 8 hours. The ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"v4.0.0"})," release holds 66 tasks ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench-repo-v400",children:"Marten et al., 2026b"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The version decides what a score means. Version 2.1 fixed 28 of the 89 tasks of version 2.0. In the maintainers' paired comparison, Claude Code with Opus 4.6 gained 12.1 points with no change to the model ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench21-2026",children:"Terminal-Bench Team, 2026"}),". Without the version number, you cannot tell whether the model or the benchmark moved a score."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["On the 4.0 leaderboard in October 2026, the top entry is Opus 5.5 in Claude Code at maximum effort, with 64.8% ± 3.1 ",e.jsx(s,{id:"tbench-leaderboard",children:"Terminal-Bench Team, n.d."}),". The best agent still fails about a third of its trials, so version 4.0 is not saturated."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{optional:!0,title:"Six more benchmarks, October 2026",accent:0,number:"46",children:[e.jsxs(t.table,{children:[e.jsx(t.thead,{children:e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Benchmark"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Measures"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Scoring"}),e.jsx(t.th,{children:"Test set"})]})}),e.jsxs(t.tbody,{children:[e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Humanity's Last Exam (HLE) ",e.jsx(s,{id:"hle2026nature",children:"Phan et al., 2026"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Expert questions across fields"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Exact answer"}),e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Public, 2,500 ",e.jsx(s,{id:"hle-site",children:"Center for AI Safety & Scale AI, n.d."})]})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["DeepSWE v1.1 ",e.jsx(s,{id:"deepswe2026",children:"Datacurve, 2026"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Long-horizon software engineering"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Behavioral tests"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Public, newly written tasks"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["AutomationBench ",e.jsx(s,{id:"automationbench2026",children:"Shepard & Salimans, 2026"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Business workflows across apps"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Final-state checks"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Held-out, 657"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["GDPval-AA ",e.jsx(s,{id:"aa-gdpval-aa",children:"Artificial Analysis, n.d.-a"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Professional deliverables"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"LLM-judge panel, Elo"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Public, 220"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["PostTrainBench ",e.jsx(s,{id:"posttrainbench2026",children:"Rank et al., 2026"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Agents doing post-training"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Benchmark gains of the trained model"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Public"})]}),e.jsxs(t.tr,{children:[e.jsxs(t.td,{children:["Arena ",e.jsx(s,{id:"chiang2024arena",children:"Chiang et al., 2024"})]}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Open-ended chat"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Human votes, Bradley-Terry"}),e.jsx(t.td,{children:"Live"})]})]})]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Each current benchmark measures one thing and scores it one way",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Humanity's Last Exam (HLE)"})," collects expert-written questions across many subjects, each with one answer checked automatically ",e.jsx(s,{id:"hle2026nature",children:"Phan et al., 2026"}),". Its 2,500 public questions were finalized on 2025-04-03, and a private set of held-out questions detects overfitting ",e.jsx(s,{id:"hle-site",children:"Center for AI Safety & Scale AI, n.d."}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"DeepSWE v1.1"})," tests coding agents on 113 long-horizon tasks written from scratch ",e.jsx(s,{id:"deepswe2026",children:"Datacurve, 2026"}),". Datacurve states that for this reason no model saw a solution during pretraining. Hand-written verifiers test the software's behavior."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"AutomationBench"}),", from Zapier, asks an agent to carry out business workflows across simulated apps and checks the final state against fixed assertions ",e.jsx(s,{id:"automationbench2026",children:"Shepard & Salimans, 2026"}),". Its leaderboard runs on a held-out set of 657 tasks, and a public set of 600 serves research. Its authors score strict pass or fail: a task counts only if every scored assertion passes. Artificial Analysis runs the held-out set with partial credit for completed objectives, and any guardrail violation sets the task's score to zero ",e.jsx(s,{id:"aa-index-v43",children:"Artificial Analysis, 2026c"}),". A number means little until you know its split and scoring rule."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"GDPval-AA"})," runs models as agents on the 220 public tasks of OpenAI's GDPval, drawn from the work of professionals in 44 occupations ",e.jsx(s,{id:"gdpval2025",children:"Patwardhan et al., 2025"}),". An LLM judge from a panel of three picks the better of two submissions blind, and the results are fitted into Elo ratings ",e.jsx(s,{id:"aa-gdpval-aa",children:"Artificial Analysis, n.d.-a"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"PostTrainBench"})," asks an agent to post-train a small base model on one H100 GPU in 10 hours and scores the trained model's benchmark gains ",e.jsx(s,{id:"posttrainbench2026",children:"Rank et al., 2026"}),". Some agents trained on test data, downloaded instruction-tuned checkpoints and used credentials they found."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Arena"})," turns human votes between two anonymous answers into ratings with a Bradley-Terry model ",e.jsx(s,{id:"chiang2024arena",children:"Chiang et al., 2024"}),". Its test set is live."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{optional:!0,title:"Nanochat's small-scale fit changes the constant",figure:e.jsx(b,{}),figureWidth:"3/5",accent:7,number:"47",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
